<section class="slide" data-i="2">
      <div class="eyebrow">Slide 3 · Baseline</div>
      <h2 class="section">A normal BPE tokenizer</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Byte Pair Encoding (BPE) is the usual way large language models build a fixed list of pieces.
        It starts from letters and repeatedly joins the most common pair of neighbouring pieces
        until the list reaches the size limit (here, 10,000).
      </p>

      <div class="flow-wrap">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 960 220" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Normal BPE flow">
          <rect width="960" height="220" fill="#f5f5f5"/>
          <!-- boxes -->
          <rect x="24" y="48" width="160" height="100" fill="#111"/>
          <text x="104" y="88" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="500">1 · Letters</text>
          <text x="104" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9e9ea0" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">every character</text>
          <text x="104" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9e9ea0" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">is a piece</text>

          <path d="M194 98 H230" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="230,92 242,98 230,104" fill="#111"/>

          <rect x="250" y="48" width="180" height="100" fill="#fff" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="340" y="88" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="500">2 · Count pairs</text>
          <text x="340" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#707072" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">find neighbouring</text>
          <text x="340" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#707072" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">pieces that co-occur most</text>

          <path d="M440 98 H476" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="476,92 488,98 476,104" fill="#111"/>

          <rect x="496" y="48" width="180" height="100" fill="#fff" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="586" y="88" text-anchor="middle" fill="#111" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="500">3 · Merge once</text>
          <text x="586" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#707072" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">join that pair into</text>
          <text x="586" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#707072" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">one new piece</text>

          <path d="M686 98 H722" stroke="#111" stroke-width="2"/>
          <polygon points="722,92 734,98 722,104" fill="#111"/>

          <rect x="742" y="48" width="190" height="100" fill="#111"/>
          <text x="837" y="88" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="500">4 · Repeat</text>
          <text x="837" y="112" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9e9ea0" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">until list has</text>
          <text x="837" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#9e9ea0" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="12">10,000 pieces</text>

          <text x="480" y="190" text-anchor="middle" fill="#707072" font-family="Inter,sans-serif" font-size="13">
            Result: almost everything is split into sub-word pieces — even common full words.
          </text>
        </svg>
      </div>

