          <p>
            For each language, count how many <strong>pieces</strong> the tokenizer needs for the whole page,
            then divide by how many <strong>words</strong> are on the page:
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:10px; font-weight:500;">
            X&nbsp;=&nbsp;pieces ÷ words
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:10px;">
            Goal: <strong>X for English ≤ 1.2</strong> (on average, English uses at most 1.2 pieces per word).
            Overall score: <strong>1000 ÷ (highest X − lowest X)</strong> across the four languages — higher is fairer.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Plain BPE on our pages (10k list)</h3>
          <table class="stats">
            <tr><th>Language</th><th>X (pieces per word)</th><th>Under 1.2?</th></tr>
