      <!-- worked mini example -->
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Tiny example — why listing a full word helps</h3>
        <p style="margin-bottom:10px;">
          Suppose the word <strong>“India”</strong> appears many times on the English page.
          Plain BPE might need several short pieces to spell it
          (for example something like <code style="background:#fff;padding:2px 6px;">In</code>
          + <code style="background:#fff;padding:2px 6px;">di</code>
          + <code style="background:#fff;padding:2px 6px;">a</code> — 3 pieces every time it shows up).
          If we put the whole string <strong>India</strong> into the 10,000-list once,
          every occurrence becomes <strong>1 piece</strong>.
          That lowers total pieces on the page (T) without changing how many words are on the page (D),
          so X = T÷D moves down toward 1.0 — and easier to stay ≤ 1.2.
        </p>
        <p class="muted">
          We do this for words across English, Hindi, Telugu and Sanskrit — not only English.
        </p>
